 34CL c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2011Fr04                           
 34CL2c  Phys Rev C 83, 048801 (2011)                                           
 34CL c  Compiled by J. Choquette and B. Singh (McMaster); April 28, 2011       
 34CL c  E(p)=200-710 keV at |?45 |mA was provided by a tandem Van de Graaff    
 34CL2c  accelerator at the University of Washington. Target consisted of       
 34CL3c  10{+16} {+33}S ions of 45 keV implanted into an oxygen-free copper     
 34CL4c  substrate. Measured E|g, I|g using two HPGe detectors at |+55|',       
 34CL5c  surrounded by plastic scintillators operating in anticoincidence       
 34CL6c  mode. Deduced stellar reaction rates for each of the three resonances, 
 34CL7c  and percentage of decays resulting in {+34}Cl g.s. and {+34m}Cl at 147.
 34CL8c  Relevance to production of sulfur isotopes and {+34m}Cl in novae       
 34CL cL $ Decay modes of g.s. and isomer are from Adopted Levels for {+34}Cl in
 34CL2cL ENSDF database                                                         
